Root cause fixed in:

- `firmware/libopencm3-examples/examples/stm32/f4/stm32f4-discovery/button/button.c`

### Root cause
The “slow while button held” delay loop had been reduced from `3000000` iterations to `500000`, so pressing the button only added a small delay and the blink looked only slightly slower.

### Fix applied
Restored the button-held delay loop back to `3000000` iterations:

```c
if (gpio_get(GPIOA, GPIO0)) {
    for (i = 0; i < 3000000; i++) { /* Wait a bit. */
        __asm__("nop");
    }
}
```

This restores the intended clearly noticeable slowdown while the button is held.
